<ul>
<li><a href="https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001519-custom-gpt-retirement-and-migration-faq" rel="noopener nofollow">OpenAI Help Center: Custom GPT retirement and migration FAQ</a>, for dates, what transfers and who can migrate.</li>
<li><a href="https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/migrate-custom-gpts" rel="noopener nofollow">ChatGPT Learn: Moving your custom GPT workflows to plugins</a>, for the steps and the comparison with plugins.</li>
<li><a href="https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8554397-creating-and-editing-gpts" rel="noopener nofollow">OpenAI Help Center: Creating and editing GPTs</a>, which notes that personal ChatGPT plans (Free, Go, Plus, Pro) can no longer create or publish new GPTs.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Not Verified</h3>
<ul>
<li>Exact migration availability per account. OpenAI's own pages give different target dates (Sep 17 and Sep 22, 2026) and say it varies by account.</li>
<li>Whether the Oct 26, 2026 creation cutoff applies the same way to every plan. OpenAI's FAQ lists it for affected Enterprise workspaces and says other plans are expected to follow the same timeline.</li>
<li>Gemini Gems have their own timeline. A guide for that is planned.</li>
</ul>
<p class="small">Not affiliated with OpenAI. This guide is general information, not legal or business advice.</p>
